{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Go forth from the ark, you and your wife.</b> But he did not do so, rather <b>Noah went out, and his sons</b>. Rabbi Yehuda and Rabbi Nechemya disagree about it: one says, because he transgressed the command regarding relations, he was degraded and separated (nistras) — measure for measure; and one says, because he added to the command, he and his sons merited [to be addressed as one] in the matter, as it is written, ״ויאמר אלקים אל נח ואל בניו לאמר״ (and Elohim said to Noah and to his sons, saying)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The word נסתרס is unusual; it likely means 'was separated' (from his wife), reflecting the tradition that Noah abstained from relations in the ark, though the exact form is textually uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:30.201215079Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}